<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>1</b></sup> Give ear to my prayer, O God; and hide not thyself from my supplication.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>2</b></sup> Attend unto me, and hear me: I mourn in my complaint, and make a noise;<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>3</b></sup> Because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked: for they cast iniquity upon me, and in wrath they hate me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>4</b></sup> My heart is sore pained within me: and the terrors of death are fallen upon me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>5</b></sup> Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me, and horror hath overwhelmed me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>6</b></sup> And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove! <i>for then</i> would I fly away, and be at rest.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>7</b></sup> Lo, <i>then</i> would I wander far off, <i>and</i> remain in the wilderness. Selah.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>8</b></sup> I would hasten my escape from the windy storm <i>and</i> tempest.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>9</b></sup> Destroy, O Lord, <i>and</i> divide their tongues: for I have seen violence and strife in the city.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>10</b></sup> Day and night they go about it upon the walls thereof: mischief also and sorrow <i>are</i> in the midst of it.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>11</b></sup> Wickedness <i>is</i> in the midst thereof: deceit and guile depart not from her streets.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>12</b></sup> For <i>it was</i> not an enemy <i>that</i> reproached me; then I could have borne <i>it</i>: neither <i>was it</i> he that hated me <i>that</i> did magnify <i>himself</i> against me; then I would have hid myself from him:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>13</b></sup> But <i>it was</i> thou, a man mine equal, my guide, and mine acquaintance.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>14</b></sup> We took sweet counsel together, <i>and</i> walked unto the house of God in company.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>15</b></sup> Let death seize upon them, <i>and</i> let them go down quick into hell: for wickedness <i>is</i> in their dwellings, <i>and</i> among them.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>16</b></sup> As for me, I will call upon God; and the LORD shall save me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>17</b></sup> Evening, and morning, and at noon, will I pray, and cry aloud: and he shall hear my voice.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>18</b></sup> He hath delivered my soul in peace from the battle <i>that was</i> against me: for there were many with me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>19</b></sup> God shall hear, and afflict them, even he that abideth of old. Selah. Because they have no changes, therefore they fear not God.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>20</b></sup> He hath put forth his hands against such as be at peace with him: he hath broken his covenant.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>21</b></sup> <i>The words</i> of his mouth were smoother than butter, but war <i>was</i> in his heart: his words were softer than oil, yet <i>were</i> they drawn swords.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>22</b></sup> Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>23</b></sup> But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee. <br />
